0044: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0045:     """
0046:     Extract the top-left or top-right 2x2 corner crop selected by the top edge clue.
0047: 
0048:     Input structure
0049:     - The input is a square color grid whose answer is one of the two 2x2 crops
0050:       touching the top edge and a grid corner.
0051:     - A repeated color on the top row, when present, acts as the primary side cue.
0052:     - Otherwise, the two top corner colors have different whole-grid frequencies.
0053: 
0054:     Rule
0055:     - If a top-row color repeats, find the repeated top-row occurrence nearest to
0056:       a left or right edge and take the 2x2 top-corner crop on that side.
0057:     - If the top row has no repeated color, compare the whole-grid frequencies of
0058:       the two top-corner colors and take the side whose corner color is rarer.
0059: 
0060:     Key insight
0061:     - The task is not asking for an arbitrary 2x2 search: the decisive information
0062:       is on the top edge, and it selects which top corner crop to keep.
0063:     """
